English translation of the original Japanese commit message:

fix(macos): propagate output-device enumeration failures

Make all_device_ids return Result instead of converting Core Audio read
failures into an empty device list. Propagate errors through
list_output_devices and uid_for_device_name using the shared
map_os_status mapping, preserving OSStatus for generic backend errors.
System capture startup returns UID lookup errors through ready_tx
instead of reporting every failure as DeviceNotFound. Callers can
distinguish no devices from enumeration or permission failure. The
public API already had an error path, so its contract is unchanged. Add
injected-reader tests for an empty list, OSStatus -1, and the 'nope'
permission error; retain the unknown-device Ok(None) check.
